 "final_text": "## Summary\n\n**Total overdue AP for USMF as of 2026-03-02: $81,262,127.02**\n\nMethod:\n1. Explored the ERP schema and found `VendorTransactions` \u2014 the posted AP subledger (dataareaid, due_date, amount, settled, closed fields). Confirmed the entity is not exposed via the SQL tool (only master data like `Vendors` is), so aggregation required paginating the full subledger via `data_find_entities`.\n2. Confirmed scope: all 3,428 rows are company USMF, `txn_type=\"Invoice\"`, `closed=0` (unsettled), `settled=0`, currency USD \u2014 no other companies, payment/credit entries, or partial settlements exist in this world.\n3. Ran a background Workflow that fanned out 18 parallel agents to paginate all 138 pages (25 rows/page) of `VendorTransactions`, filtering each row for `due_date < 2026-03-02` and returning raw `{id, amount, due_date}` tuples \u2014 summation was done in deterministic JS (not LLM arithmetic) to guarantee exactness.\n4. Ran 16 independent spot-check agents that re-fetched sampled pages from scratch and compared against the primary fetch \u2014 **zero mismatches**, row coverage 3,428/3,428, cross-check diff $0.00.\n5. Result: 3,202 of 3,428 invoices are overdue, totaling **$81,262,127.02**.\n\nSubmitted `total_overdue_ap: 81262127.02` and `as_of_date: \"2026-03-02\"` via the harness.",
